    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d746">

                <pb facs="0990" n="880" xml:id="pg880"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.5212A/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hammond</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-12T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 12,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>26. The Department handed the Spanish Ambassador on March 12, a draft of a
                    proposed Treaty of Arbitration between the United States and Spain. The
                    provisions of the draft operate to extend the policy of arbitration enunciated
                    in the Root Treaty of April 20, 1908, which expired June 2, 1923. The language
                    of the draft is identical in effect with that of the arbitration treaty recently
                    signed with France and with the draft arbitration treaties already submitted to
                    the Norwegian, British, Japanese, Italian and German Governments.<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d746-f1"/> The text of the proposed treaty will be forwarded in the
                    next pouch.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d746-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d746-f1" n="54" xml:id="d746-f1-content">
                <p>For negotiations with Germany and Great Britain, see <ref
                        target="frus1928v02#pg_862">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, pp.
                        862</ref> ff., and <ref target="frus1928v02#pg_943">pp. 943</ref> ff.; with
                    Italy and Japan, see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg102">pp.
                        102</ref> ff. and <ref target="#pg135">pp. 135</ref> ff. Although
                    negotiations with Norway were instituted in 1928, the treaty was not signed
                    until 1929 (Department of State Treaty Series No. 788).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d746-f2" n="55" xml:id="d746-f2-content">
                <p>Draft treaty not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
